course: dictionary
lesson: 12960
title: Getting rid of waste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body makes waste all the time, and it must get rid of it to stay healthy. Getting rid of waste is called excretion. «Excretion keeps the body clean inside.» Here the word means removing waste that the body has made.
explain: Your kidneys make urine, which carries waste out of your body. Your skin lets out sweat when you get hot. Your lungs breathe out carbon dioxide each time you breathe out. These three are organs of excretion, meaning they are the parts that do the job.
explain: Excretion is not only for people. «Animals and plants also get rid of waste from their bodies.» Think of excretion as the body taking out its rubbish, just as your house puts its bin out on the street.
fact: Excretion means getting rid of waste that the body has made.
fact: Urine, sweat and carbon dioxide are examples of waste that the body excretes.
fact: The kidneys, lungs and skin are organs of excretion.
fact: An excretion is one waste substance that is passed out of a living thing.
fact: Excretion is one of the seven life processes, remembered as MRS GREN.
exercise: Which body part is an organ of excretion? | Ears | *Kidneys | Heart | Hair
exercise: Which of these is a waste gas that the body excretes? | Oxygen that we breathe in | Food we eat | *Carbon dioxide | Water we drink
exercise: Which of these is also one of the life processes in MRS GREN? | Shopping | *Growth | Watching television
test: «The lungs breathe out carbon dioxide, which is a waste gas.» What does this sentence tell us about the lungs? | They store food | They pump blood | *They take part in excretion | They help the body grow tall
test: Mia says excretion means eating food. What does excretion really mean? | *Getting rid of waste the body has made | Moving from one place to another | Taking in food and drink | Making new living things
exam: Which of these is an example of an excretion? | *Sweat | Sleep | Sunlight | Breakfast
